      "side": 1,
      "message": "I left some minor comments but I am starting to realize that if ridders method is being used, then isn\u0027t it the case that just want a large relative_step_size and then the min_step_size is also the relative_step_size if we are using ridders method?\n\nwhy do we even need the ridders_min_initial_step_size anymore? is it going to have a value other than the relative_step_size?",
