      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T07:09:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would first distinguish that the `relative_step_size` is a multiplier and the `min_step_size` or `ridders_min_initial_step_size` are absolute values. \nTherefore I think it is hard to say \"lets set a large relative_step_size\" when we use ridders, because there is no guarantee about the parameter magnitude being multiplied.\n\nYour general sentiment seems correct and I agree. My vote would be to provide two parameters for all numerical diff options:\n\n1) `relative_step_size`\n2) `min_step_size`\n\nI am not an expert in numerical differentiation, but the semantics of only allowing the user to set a minimum step size for the ridder case just seems a little confusing. That being said, I think the current patchset stands on its own fixing a bug, and I would be hesitant to pack this change on too. \n\nThanks for your time and thought and sorry for the delay!\n\nJack",
      "parentUuid": "a3714bd0_dd7e640f",
      "revId": "c3c042592bc81c5e4ca8c3d068468cf1359f06cd",
      "serverId": "cdcfcfbe-2044-3b1f-b5d4-da77ad542329"
