      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did this in a draft, but then realized that we then loose the protection of the sqrt(eps) for the case when ridders method is selected. \n\nIf your main goal is to enforce constness then we can do the following, which is a little more verbose and keeps the min step size \"protected\" also in the ridders case.\n\n\n```\nconst double min_allowed_step_size \u003d std::sqrt(std::numeric_limits\u003cdouble\u003e::epsilon());\n  \nconst double min_step_size \u003d kMethod \u003d\u003d RIDDERS? std::max(ridders_min_initial_step_size, min_allowed_step_size) : min_allowed_step_size;\n```\n\nI know the user should never pass a small value for the ridders step size, but it feels wrong to only half enforce the sqrt(eps) invariant mentioned in the comment.",
